 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186271067 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271757 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271757 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271757 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186270443 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271757 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8d0ebc5f-e6ef-575e-b450-25f928dd50ea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271984 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186271757 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271984 #edb/ref 1069 "q-139970" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271984 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271984 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $W$ be a $9\\times 10$ matrix that has $8$ pivot columns. What is the dimension of the null space of $W?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271984 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a4bb5b4f-d3a8-5ac1-8e9b-25b93297fd4c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271984 #edb/ref 1074 "We know that $\\text{dim(Null}(W))$ is the number of non-pivot columns in $W.$ \n\nSince $W$ has $10$ columns and $8$ of them are pivots, then the number of non-pivot columns in $W$ is \n\n$$\n10-8=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{dim(Null}(W))=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271986 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186271646 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271986 #edb/ref 1069 "q-139973" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271986 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271986 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. If $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.$\n\nII. If $B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\,0\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.$\n\nIII. If $C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(C))=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271986 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c75ae37f-79fb-5023-b676-a4acf7953ba3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271986 #edb/ref 1074 "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The matrix $B$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $3$rd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. The matrix $C$ has $3$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271988 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186271578 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271988 #edb/ref 1069 "q-139975" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271988 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271988 #edb/ref 1071 "If $W=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 4 & 9 \\\\ 5 & -20 & 10 & 8\\end{aligned}],\\,$ then $\\text{nullity}(W)=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271988 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "59f4ef86-ac62-591e-aa5f-05de601f1524" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271988 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that by definition, $\\text{nullity}(W)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(W)).$\n\nTo find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(W))$, we reduce $W$ to row echelon form, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 12 & 4 & 9 \\\\ 5 & -20 & 10 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 10 & 18 \\\\ 5 & -20 & 10 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 10 & 18 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns and  $1$\n non-pivot column (the $2$nd). \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(W)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(W))=1.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317749 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317749 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317749 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "38fc6530-da0e-5ef8-9489-487b09a244dc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317854 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317854 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317854 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "56588881-20d6-50d9-9ff9-b07f78c8d62a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317966 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317966 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317966 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "74eb3b2a-e28b-5f5f-8bad-16800439d2bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318213 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318213 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318213 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c40e8a26-c0ea-5391-8ea7-86af9f58fbcf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318281 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318281 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318281 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d79b5d41-92e6-55a5-93af-01f4431ff8c9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318941 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186317749 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318941 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186317854 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318941 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186317966 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318941 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186318213 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318941 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186318281 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318941 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318941 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318941 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186317966 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186318941 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f7f6e57d-01d6-53e7-aeb3-fe75d269ce0e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319406 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319406 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045