n{aligned}2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321072 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "da3efbc4-2fa4-54a8-9aa9-e1c2c723490a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321072 #edb/ref 1074 "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has $3$ pivot columns and no non-pivot column. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has $1$ pivot column and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $4$th column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C))=0+1+1=2.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321134 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320510 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321134 #edb/ref 1069 "q-35348" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321134 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321134 #edb/ref 1071 "Given $Z=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 12 & 3 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -7 & 11 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 7 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 2 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,$ what is $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(Z))?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321134 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a52db54f-ed58-568b-ad92-d2a1074b04ad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321134 #edb/ref 1074 "To find $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(Z))$, we reduce $Z$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Z & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 12 & 3 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -7 & 11 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 7 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 2 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{3}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 12 & 3 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -7 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 7 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 2 & -4 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{5} & :={R}_{5}+(-\\frac{2}{3}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 12 & 3 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -7 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 12 & 3 & -6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -7 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $4$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $4$th column). \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(Z))=1.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345611 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345611 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345611 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1e0e3b4d-76d8-5cbd-90c5-fca2f4d2fe65" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345618 #edb/ref 1080 "6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345618 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345618 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1e90027c-95de-50a1-8923-ce31ce3d2313" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345786 #edb/ref 1080 "9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345786 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345786 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "312c6d20-1c2c-5d6c-8b8e-cf23e71760b6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345902 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345902 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345902 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4038465c-abf2-5ed6-9c88-95500bd0b19f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345962 #edb/ref 1080 "8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345962 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345962 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "45f68372-7412-515e-9814-e6c0f7a8c6df" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345978 #edb/ref 1080 "7" #ed